Currently, this code will incorrectly emit error:

```
shader_type spatial;

void fragment()
{
	switch(0)
	{
		case 0:
			{
				break; // ERROR HERE
			}
	}
}
```
By checking blocks recursively I solved this problem.

Added function to expose floor normal, useful to correctly calculate the player velocity.

@akien-mga Add an API is not allowed in feature frezes, so it could not be added in the 3.2 version. But let me say that without the `floor_normal` correctly calculate the player velocity is not so easy, so I say that this should be considered to be part of 3.2.

This work has been kindly sponsored by IMVU.

Exposed:
```cpp
