```

Fix #35149

This huge PR enables the 'struct' keyword and its usage in the shaders. Target to close https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/301
Implemented and worked:

- nested struct instances
```
struct A {
 vec3 color;
};
struct B {
 A a;
 int b;
};
```
- struct constructors
```
B b = B(A(vec3(1.0, 0.0, 1.0)), 1);
```
- struct arrays
```
	A test[] = {A(vec3(1, 1, 1))};
	ALBEDO = test[0].color;
```
- struct constant instances (at global scope too)
`const A test = A(vec3(1.0));`
- struct as functions parameters and return type
```
A test(A a, in B b)
{
	A t;
	t.color = vec3(1, 1, 0) + a.color / b.a.color * float(b.b);
	return t;
}
```
- correct intellisense support (demo screenshot)
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/3036176/72641926-4f74bd00-397c-11ea-91d2-ff467e9a3c11.png)

Not implemented:
- global struct instances like:
```
struct L {
//...
} instance1, instance2; // <- these instances
```
I noticed @reduz don't want such global values because they may confuse other users.

`master` version of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/48450.

I managed to sort out the alignment issues mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/24317#issuecomment-576074059. The appearance is now almost identical to the original, except that version identifiers are now clickable in the Project Manager, the editor's bottom panel and About dialog. All three buttons will copy the same text (full version identifier with hash for Git builds).

